in the last hour it's been announced the  2030 asian games will be held in  doha the qatari capital was revealed as  the venue by the olympic council of asia  while riyadh was named as the host of  the 2034 games  under a compromise agreed between qatar  and saudi arabia  the games are the second biggest  multi-sport event after the olympics  let's get more now with our sports  presenter andy richardson andy so both  countries had wanted to host in 2030.  how was the solution reached  well i think uh it's a victory really  for for doha and qatar's long-term  commitment to its sporting  infrastructure i mean it's  it's hard of course and not to see that  the geopolitics of this situation with  saudi arabia being part of the blockade  that's been imposed on qatar but i think  this is slightly more nuanced and  perhaps slightly more straightforward  than that qatar has vast experience of  hosting  uh huge sporting events it started  really in 2006 when it hosted the asian  games  for the first time it's remodeled its  national stadium  and everything really is in place to  re-host an asian games and since then  last year we saw the world athletics  championships hosted  here in doha and of course the big one  coming around the corner the football  world cup and that has resulted in  even more investment in training  facilities  in uh transport facilities for for fans  and media  so it's already there and the scale of  this event is hard to understate  it is the second biggest multi-sport  event after the olympics it will involve  ten thousand plus athletes um and the  olympics uh the olympic association uh  at both regional level and the  international level  by thomas back is it pains to stress  that it doesn't want to overburden  hosting countries and at the moment  qatar is in a position  where pretty much tomorrow it could host  these asian games  has to be said that riyadh and saudi  arabia are also moving in that direction  they are starting to host big sporting  events be it  a formula one race next year they've  hosted uh big boxing matches in the last  few months as well but in terms of  hosting multi-sport events with  large numbers of international athletes  it isn't quite there yet so  this compromise has been reached whereby  saudi arabia will be given that extra  few years to prepare for the 2034 asian  games  you sort of touched on it there andy but  i'm wondering if you can talk to us a  little bit more  about the wider context here  yeah of course um there is uh the the  blockade that's been imposed uh  on qatar by neighbouring countries  including saudi arabia is of course part  of the conversation  uh that's in the background here and  it's arguable that perhaps uh rihanna  wouldn't have been pushed into  into bidding so soon for an asian games  had it not been for the fact that their  their great regional rivals doha were  also going for the  for the 20 30 games there's also um a  desire to to bring the olympics one day  um to the middle east and and which  country will be at the front of the race  to do that  now doha is is very keen and to uh to  put itself forward  for 2032. um it's bid a couple of times  in the past  um the big stumbling block it will face  is  is the timing of the olympics with the  asian games  uh the organizers can be a bit more  flexible for example when doha hosted  in 2006 the games were hosted in  december  um when the weather is is much cooler  here um the olympics  they are very sort of determined to  always have the olympics hosted  june july august number of reasons for  that one of the main reasons being that  the main  source of income for the olympics um is  a huge contract they have with nbc  in the united states uh they want the  games to be hosted  in the summer they don't want it to be  clashing with major north american  sporting leagues later on in the year  when the middle east  would like to host an olympics be in  october november december but the ioc  the international olympic committee  had indicated they wanted to see doha  host another big  sporting event after the world cup  something like the asian games before  they rebid  for the olympics so this is the perfect  opportunity for that  what doha wants is some kind of  commitment that there is some  wiggle room as to when they can host the  olympics um but 2032 is a very realistic  bid  bid schedule now for doha to try and  bring the olympics to the middle east  for the first time as well  okay thank you for that sports presenter  andy richardson
 

